{"id":"u-428fc647-1821-49a7-b659-114165f65896","src":"community","title":"God's Chosen Program","author":"João Marques","url":"https://www.boostcamp.app/users/n2zSIh-ppl-2x-high-effort-hypertrophy-1","desc":"This program is designed for intermediate lifters who enjoy bodybuilding style training, hard sets, and relatively high training frequency. It is best suited to lifters with above average work capacity and recovery.\nThe foundation is a complete six day push/pull/legs split. An optional seventh day adds extra shoulder, trap, calf, and core volume, but is not required for the program to be complete.\nThe program provides substantial training volume for the chest, back, legs, shoulders, and arms, with additional emphasis on the posterior chain. Multiple movement patterns and resistance profiles are used to develop each muscle without relying on unnecessary exercise redundancy.\nCompound lifts provide measurable long-term progression, while carefully selected isolation exercises add targeted hypertrophy work. Chest training includes incline, flat, dip, machine, and fly variations. Back training combines vertical pulls, rows, and shoulder extension work. Lower body training covers squatting, hinging, unilateral work, knee flexion, and hip extension.\nMost exercises use a relatively small number of hard working sets performed close to failure. Higher fatigue movements such as squats, deadlifts, RDLs, and walking lunges use more conservative effort targets where appropriate.\nThe combination of six main training days, substantial weekly volume, and frequent hard sets can still be demanding, so volume should be adjusted to the individual when necessary. If recovery, performance, sleep, or motivation begins to decline, skip the optional seventh day first. After that, the third compound movement on a Push, Pull, or Legs day can be treated as optional accessory work and removed when needed. Isolation work for smaller muscle groups, such as the biceps and triceps, can also be occasionally skipped or trimmed. If further reduction is needed, some main compound movements can be reduced from three working sets to two.\nThe priority is to preserve high quality, high effort training rather than complete every prescribed set at the expense of recovery. Supersets are used selectively for compatible accessory movements to save time without compromising performance on the major lifts.\nThe goal is simple, train hard, recover well, progressively improve performance, and build a balanced, muscular physique.","level":["Advanced","Intermediate"],"goals":["Muscle","Bodyweight Fitness"],"equipment":["Full Gym"],"minutes":90,"joins":5,"rate":0,"rateCount":0,"updated":"2026-09-10T11:02:02.800Z","variations":[{"name":"default","days":["Pull A","Push A","Legs A","Shoulders + Core (Extra Day)","Pull B","Push B","Legs B"],"weeks":[[{"ex":[{"n":"Underhand Lat Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Barbell Row","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":9,"x":3}]},{"n":"Single Arm Row (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"ss":[{"n":"Face Pull","sets":[{"lo":15,"hi":25,"rpe":6,"rpeHi":8,"x":2}],"note":"Shoulder health focus — keep it controlled, pull toward face/upper chest, externally rotate, squeeze rear delts/upper back, and stop before form degrades. Do not take to failure."},{"n":"Straight Arm Pulldown","sets":[{"lo":10,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]}]},{"n":"Incline Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Hammer Curl (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":12,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Shrug (Barbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]}]},{"ex":[{"n":"Incline Bench Press (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Dip (Weighted)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":3}]},{"n":"Chest Press (Machine)","sets":[{"lo":6,"hi":10,"rpe":9,"rpeHi":10,"x":2}]},{"n":"Chest Fly (Dumbbell)","sets":[{"lo":8,"hi":15,"rpe":8